        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="0707" n="617" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg617"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115/14331</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-03"><hi rendition="#italic">September 3,
                        1918</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 18.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 9821</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my telegram No. 1418 of
                    August 27, 5 p.m., in regard to the desire of the United States Government to
                    obtain <pb facs="0708" n="618" xml:id="pg618"/> the release of various American
                    goods which have been seized by the British Authorities, I now have the honor to
                    transmit herewith to the Department, a copy of the Note, dated August 24, 1918,
                    which I have received from the Foreign Office, together with a copy of the
                    revised list of goods referred to therein.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d511-f1"/></p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Irwin
                            Laughlin</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d511-a1.xml" xpointer="d511-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d511-f1" n="17" xml:id="d511-f1-content">
                <p>List of goods not printed.</p>
